<title>SWEDEN: SWIMMING-VOELKER BREAKS EUROPEAN 50 FREESTYLE RECORD.</title>
<headline>SWIMMING-VOELKER BREAKS EUROPEAN 50 FREESTYLE RECORD.</headline>
<dateline>GOTHENBURG, Sweden 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sandra Voelker of Germany broke her own European women's 50 metres freestyle short -course record at the world short-course swimming championships on Friday.</p>
<p>Voelker clocked 24.62 seconds to lead qualifiers in the morning heats, beating the 24.67 she set at the European short-course championships in Rostock on December 14 last year.</p>
